From 9c943cbd2f1c3cb1717f36d1ac9eb81fd0e8f880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:13:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): bind a pinned model's provider at pin time,
 refuse when ambiguous [daveey]

A concrete model pinned with no provider late-bound its provider to the
profile's config.yaml at every spawn. When that config briefly read
class:deep / provider auto, the auto ladder sent claude-opus-5-5 to
OpenRouter (HTTP 400, exit 78) on a card whose earlier runs had worked.

hermes_cli/kanban_pin_provider.resolve_pin_provider is now the one
resolver for create_task and set_model_override (so kanban_create, hermes
kanban create --model, set-model and the dashboard): the profile's
model.provider when it serves the id, else the single authenticated
provider whose catalog lists it (vendor first-party as fallback). None or
several -> pin_provider_unresolved naming the providers to pass. Class
selectors are unchanged. The dispatcher binds legacy NULL-provider rows
with the same resolver and records it on the model_tier event.
---
